course: dictionary
lesson: 10286
title: Words that travel
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words travel between countries and change their meaning on the way. Context tells you which meaning is right. «Flatbreads like pitta and tortilla are made without yeast» shows that here a tortilla is a kind of bread, not an egg dish.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Pitta gets its pocket because water inside turns to steam in a hot oven» is about bread, so the other flatbread in that sentence is bread too. Ask yourself: what does the rest of the sentence tell me about this word?
explain: Some words have two meanings. Tortilla is a flat bread from Mexico, but in Spain it can mean a thick omelette. A good check is to swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A tortilla is a thin, flat, round bread made from maize (corn) or wheat flour, from Mexico.
fact: In Spain, a tortilla is a thick omelette made with eggs and potatoes.
fact: «Tortillas are usually made from maize», so a corn tortilla is a common kind.
fact: Tortillas are used for tacos, wraps and burritos, and tortilla chips are a common snack.
fact: «Pitta» and «tortilla» are both flatbreads made without yeast.
exercise: «Flatbreads like pitta and tortilla are made without yeast.» What is a tortilla in this sentence? | *A flat bread | A type of potato | A sweet cake | A thick omelette
exercise: «Tortillas are usually made from maize.» What is maize? | A sort of potato | A flour made only from wheat | A cheese from Spain | *Another name for corn
exercise: Ella says a tortilla in Spain is a bread. What is a tortilla in Spain? | A taco shell | A flat, round bread | *A thick omelette made with eggs and potatoes | A type of sweet
test: «Pitta puffs up only because water inside turns to steam.» What makes pitta puff up? | *Water turning to steam in a hot oven | Yeast | Salt | Sugar
test: Which food is usually made from maize? | Sponge cake | *Tortilla | Pitta | Pasta
exam: Jayden reads «Pasta is made from wheat, and tortillas are usually made from maize.» What does tortilla mean here, and which clue helped? | A bowl of rice, because rice is food | A thick omelette, because pasta is eggy | A sweet cake, because wheat is sweet | *A flat bread, because it is made from maize
